Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-162: laptop package 129's designer part merged
 into the machine tree -- ES02's 0.162 (0.162.0)

GitHub main aab3911 (GitLab 13a57384), mixed; its C++ / web part = the integration session's 43580b0 (cpp 0141).
Three-way on the package's base_116a0809 (= package 128, which carried no designer files), against the tree as it is
now, CRLF to LF first: package.json, WPF_DIFF_LOG.md, lib/cppstub.js, test/e2e_build.js changed only by ES02 (copied
byte for byte); CHANGELOG.md, extension.js, HANDOVER.md, test/smoke_extension.js on both sides (git merge-file, no
conflict). The machine's own patches kept: tools 0136, 0143, 0145, 0147 (the F5 build bar).
ES02's 0.162: deleting an event (the events table's Reset) first shows what goes -- the page's htdCpp line, the
dispatch row, the C++ handler (.h declaration, .cpp body) -- and deletes them together; the handler is kept, with the
reason, when something else calls it, another event uses it, or it is not the designer's and has code in it.
Tests: lib 181/181, probe 7/7 + tab tree 7/7, extension 224/224, panels all pass; real VS Code 156/159 (the 3 known
"Pages" list checks); e2e_build.ps1 not run.

